[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3617283202","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113629#issuecomment-3617283202","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113629","id":3617283202,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Xm1yC","user":{"login":"RandomShaper","id":11797174,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk3MTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11797174?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper","html_url":"https://github.com/RandomShaper","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-05T15:03:42Z","updated_at":"2025-12-05T15:03:42Z","body":"I moved the lock to the beginning of the fuction because `flush_read_ptr` wouldn't otherwise be safely accessed. I guess the fix then is the other approach you describe: using a (non-binary, that is, recursive) `Mutex`. I chose a binary one when I saw no need for recursivity. However, now there is. 😀","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3617283202/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3617365315","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113629#issuecomment-3617365315","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113629","id":3617365315,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7XnJ1D","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-05T15:25:29Z","updated_at":"2025-12-05T15:25:29Z","body":"I tried changing `CommandQueueMT::mutex` to be a `Mutex` instead, but it seems there's a bunch of code related to the \"unlock allowance zones\" in `WorkerThreadPool` that expects a `std::mutex`, as opposed to a `std::recursive_mutex`.\r\n\r\nI'll go ahead and close this for the reason mentioned above. I'd prefer if someone more familiar with this code made the switch from `BinaryMutex` to `Mutex` instead.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3617365315/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3617426651","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113629#issuecomment-3617426651","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113629","id":3617426651,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7XnYzb","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-05T15:41:09Z","updated_at":"2025-12-05T15:41:48Z","body":"I guess as a quick hack this PR could also just slap a `thread_local` on `CommandQueueMT::flush_read_ptr`, since I can't really see a reason why that member needs to be shared between threads in the first place. That would resolve any race condition concerns, and still allow the lock guard to be placed after the reentrancy check.\r\n\r\nBut switching to `Mutex` is likely the better (albeit more laborious) fix.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3617426651/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3618245490","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113629#issuecomment-3618245490","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113629","id":3618245490,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Xqgty","user":{"login":"brycehutchings","id":5100250,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMDAyNTA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5100250?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings","html_url":"https://github.com/brycehutchings","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-05T19:20:23Z","updated_at":"2025-12-05T19:20:23Z","body":"> I tried changing `CommandQueueMT::mutex` to be a `Mutex` instead, but it seems there's a bunch of code related to the \"unlock allowance zones\" in `WorkerThreadPool` that expects a `std::mutex`, as opposed to a `std::recursive_mutex`.\r\n> \r\n> I'll go ahead and close this for the reason mentioned above. I'd prefer if someone more familiar with this code made the switch from `BinaryMutex` to `Mutex` instead.\r\n\r\nI'm new to this code, but I'm still confused by these lock allowance zones / non-unique flusher. If only one thread can actively flush because of the mutex+flush_read_ptr early check, why can't the other consumers of the command queue use unique_flusher=true mode (really get rid of unique_flusher=false support) now that we unlock during command invocation? The only difference I can see is that when unique_flusher=false, the command queue might still block other threads that want to queue commands.\r\n\r\nI say this because it sounds like if the lock allowance zones feature could be removed, it'd be trivial to switch to a recursive mutex to resolve this problem.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3618245490/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]